# Go build output
/dossierx
/dossierx.exe
*.exe
/dist/

# Test/coverage output
*.out
coverage.html

# Engine artifacts left behind by running the CLI against a project checked
# out inside this tree. "dossierx check" writes build/ledger/comment-digest.json
# under a project's build directory, and outside testdata/ that is a
# regenerable dropping. Unanchored (the leading **) so it catches the repo
# root and any project checked out inside this tree; a pattern containing a
# slash is otherwise anchored to the directory holding this file. A real
# consuming project commits its own digest; its .gitignore is its own.
**/build/ledger/comment-digest.json

# ...but NOT under testdata/. The engine now REFUSES an ignored store
# (store-gitignored, checked per file with --no-index against this
# repository's own .gitignore), and this repository runs the engine on its own
# fixtures in place: the five rendered fixtures through `dossierx check`, and
# the 41 projects under testdata/fixture-coverage through `check --validate`
# (tests/lint_fixtures_test.go, tests/lifecycle_fixtures_test.go). Every fixture
# digest is therefore a tracked fixture input. The negation must be `**`, not
# `*`: a `*` does not cross `/`, so it would re-include only fixtures one level
# down and leave every fixture-coverage project reporting store-gitignored.
!testdata/**/build/ledger/comment-digest.json

# The fixtures' lock stores and build orders need no negation here because no
# pattern in this file ever ignored one.

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

